The repair will use a local transaction journal plus signing-key rotation: each committed generation gets a new 32-byte signing key, so restoring older data/auth bytes without restoring the current signing authority fails; the journal records and authenticates the prior tuple so interruptions roll back to the last committed generation. I’ll keep the existing raw key shape and state schema number required by protected tests, but advance the recovery contract/auth schema so the pre-repair state cannot be silently reinterpreted.
Frozen refs/hashes and the locked baseline are verified. Implementation is scoped to the three v02 modules and the two allowed integrity-test modules.
  → Implement signing-authority freshness, durable transaction recovery, private state reads, current-literature reloads, and structured source identity
  • Add red/green integrity regressions for all six blocking findings
  • Run focused tests, inspect diff/scope, then run the exact supervisor validation and write the structured return
